<%# Author: powered by stimulus-autocomplete instead of the vendored
    typeahead.js/Bloodhound widget - the first field to use the shared
    autocomplete partial. Label, title, dom ids, param names and the
    wrapper's "author" class are all kept as they were, so the GUI is
    unchanged; only the JS driving the dropdown is different.

    Server-side resolution (Name::AsResolvedTypeahead::ForAuthor) is
    untouched - it doesn't know or care which JS widget populated these
    fields, including the typed-exact-match-without-a-pick case.

    dependents_field mirrors the setDependents('author-by-abbrev') call the
    old typeahead.js wiring made after a pick. Nothing in the app currently
    declares .requires-author-by-abbrev or .hide-if-author-by-abbrev, so it
    is a no-op today; passed through for exact fidelity with the old
    behaviour. %>
<%= render "shared/autocomplete_field",
           f: f,
           id_attribute: :author_id,
           input_id: "author-by-abbrev",
           input_name: "name[author_typeahead]",
           input_value: @name.author.try("abbrev_if_possible"),
           label: "#{"Original " if @name.changed_combination}Author",
           title: "Authors will be suggested as you type, so please select from the list or type enough to identify a single author by abbreviation.",
           url: authors_typeahead_on_abbrev_html_path,
           wrapper_class: "author",
           dependents_field: "author-by-abbrev" %>
